   "spoken": "Here's a principle for disarming any gambit. Grabbing the second pawn is best by the engine's cold count — there just isn't enough compensation. But in practice the middle path is often wiser: hand the pawn back and, in return, claim a development lead. Stop worrying about clinging to the extra material and just get pieces out.",
   "kind": "plan"
