   "ply": 8,
   "t": 115.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/ppp1pppp/2n2n2/8/3Pp3/2N2P2/PPP3PP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The developing move that also bites is the knight to c6 — it counterattacks the loose pawn. The natural-looking bishop development isn't as good as it seems, because a pawn thrust to d5 would kick the knight and hand over the e5 outpost.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
