   "line": [
    "Nb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight jump to b5 is pure intimidation — the sort of scary-looking move that concrete calculation keeps you safe from. Ask the obvious question: is there any reason not to just take the knight? The only pause is that the queens could come off and the king lose its castling — but two pawns up, with pieces trading, a king in the centre is a long way from getting mated.",
   "kind": "tactic"
