   "spoken": "This is a classic trap the opponent falls into — expecting an in-between check followed by a leisurely capture. What they've missed is that a single knight move to d6 does two jobs at once: it saves the knight and blocks the check. Two pawns and a piece to the good, the rest is technique.",
